---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import CodeCard from '../../components/CodeCard.astro';
---
<Base title="Use it" description="Run OpenJevX and wire it into jevx.">
  <h1>Use it</h1>
  <p class="lead">One server, one endpoint: <code>POST /v1/systemone</code>. Everything below assumes
    the default port <code>21118</code>.</p>

  <h2>Run it</h2>
  <CodeCard label="macOS / Linux">npx git+https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx.git
openjevx</CodeCard>
  <p>or download a package for your platform from the{' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/latest">latest release</a>:</p>
  <CodeCard label="macOS">curl -L -O https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/download/v0.5.8/openjevx-darwin-arm64.tar
curl -L -O https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/download/v0.5.8/openjevx-model-0.5.2.tar.gz
tar -xf openjevx-darwin-arm64.tar && tar -xzf openjevx-model-0.5.2.tar.gz && ./openjevx</CodeCard>
  <CodeCard label="Linux">curl -L -O https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/download/v0.5.8/openjevx-linux-amd64.tar
curl -L -O https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/download/v0.5.8/openjevx-model-0.5.2.tar.gz
tar -xf openjevx-linux-amd64.tar && tar -xzf openjevx-model-0.5.2.tar.gz && ./openjevx</CodeCard>
  <p>Linux on ARM (arm64): use <a href="https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/download/v0.5.8/openjevx-linux-arm64.tar">openjevx-linux-arm64.tar</a> instead.</p>
  <p>Windows: download and run{' '}
    <a href="https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/download/v0.5.8/openjevx-windows-amd64.zip">openjevx-windows-amd64.zip</a> with <a href="https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/download/v0.5.8/openjevx-model-0.5.2.tar.gz">openjevx-model-0.5.2.tar.gz</a> unpacked into the same folder.</p>

  <h2>Docker</h2>
  <CodeCard label="Docker">docker run -d -p 127.0.0.1:21118:21118 \
  -e OPENJEVX_PASSWORD=&lt;12+ characters&gt; -e OPENJEVX_API_KEY=&lt;16+ characters&gt; \
  ghcr.io/deemwar-products/openjevx:v0.5.9</CodeCard>
  <p>The prebuilt image is for linux/amd64 and linux/arm64. To build it yourself:</p>
  <CodeCard label="Docker (from source)">git clone https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx.git && cd openjevx
OPENJEVX_PASSWORD=&lt;12+ characters&gt; OPENJEVX_API_KEY=&lt;16+ characters&gt; docker compose up -d --build</CodeCard>
  <p>The image has no default credentials and refuses to start without both. It runs as a non-root user.</p>

  <h2>Wire it into jevx</h2>
  <CodeCard label="shell">jevx profile add openjevx http://127.0.0.1:21118/v1/systemone --model openjevx
jevx profile use openjevx

jevx is "Is this urgent?" &lt; email.txt
jevx pick "Which team?" web=frontend api=backend billing=money --in "charged twice"
jevx ask --noul out_of_stock="Is the item out of stock?" --in '&#123;"stock_units": 0&#125;'</CodeCard>
  <p>A server that listens beyond <code>127.0.0.1</code> needs an API key: add{' '}
    <code>--header 'Authorization: Bearer $OPENJEVX_API_KEY'</code> to <code>jevx profile add</code>.</p>

  <h2>Config</h2>
  <p><code>openjevx.json</code> next to the binary:</p>
  <CodeCard label="openjevx.json">&#123;
  "listen": "127.0.0.1:21118",
  "device": "auto"
&#125;</CodeCard>
  <p><code>device</code> is <code>auto</code> (the first GPU provider that loads: CUDA, CoreML on macOS, DirectML on
    Windows; else CPU), <code>cpu</code>, or <code>gpu</code> (no fallback).</p>
  <h2>Credentials</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>"password"</code> (or <code>OPENJEVX_PASSWORD</code>) guards the dashboard. There is no default: unset,
      the server generates one on first start into <code>openjevx.password</code> beside <code>openjevx.json</code>.</li>
    <li><code>"api_key"</code> (or <code>OPENJEVX_API_KEY</code>) guards <code>POST /v1/systemone</code>, sent as{' '}
      <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;key&gt;</code>. Off on <code>127.0.0.1</code>; on when the server listens on
      any other address, generated into <code>openjevx.api-key</code> if unset.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Dashboard and stats</h2>
  <p>Open <code>http://127.0.0.1:21118/</code> while it runs — request counts, input tokens,
    latency p50/p95/p99, errors, recent requests.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>GET /stats</code> — JSON snapshot (password-protected)</li>
    <li><code>GET /metrics</code> — Prometheus format (password-protected)</li>
    <li><code>GET /health</code> — open, no password</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Downloads</h2>
  <div class="cards">
    <div class="card"><h3>Releases</h3><p><a href="https://github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/latest">github.com/muthuishere/openjevx/releases/latest</a></p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Hugging Face</h3><p><a href="https://huggingface.co/muthuishere/openjevx">huggingface.co/muthuishere/openjevx</a> — full precision + quantized weights</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>jevx CLI</h3><p><a href="https://github.com/muthuishere/jevx">github.com/muthuishere/jevx</a></p></div>
  </div>
</Base>
